2026-10-09T02:14:08.9026894Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9110947Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9119534Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9120270Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9120873Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9121156Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9121679Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9122404Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9122748Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9123073Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9123559Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9123773Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9124319Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9124993Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9125565Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9125903Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9126213Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9126445Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9126664Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9126884Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9127181Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9127290Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9127388Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9127514Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9127816Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9128226Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9131750Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9131866Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9132013Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9132254Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9132773Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9133318Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9133806Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9134130Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9134475Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9135104Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9135550Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9145963Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9146882Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9156776Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9157504Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9157835Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9158650Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9159149Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9174113Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9174821Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9183204Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9183846Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9184221Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9184382Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9184604Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9184878Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9185200Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9185808Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9186150Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9186291Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9186555Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9186692Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9186866Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9187148Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:08.9187271Z 
